ratios"]],"deck":2,"blurb":"Every climb in Insurmountable is different, since this roguelike generates its mountains procedurally and ends your run for good if the climber dies. You pick one of three characters, each with their own skills and backstory, then keep vital stats out of the danger zone while searching crates, caves and old ruins for gear left by earlier adventurers.\n\nWeather changes, day turns to night and random events add uncertainty, since you never know how an encounter will end. You descend as well as ascend, and every decision can matter. Single-player, aimed at players who enjoy tense survival and resource management and who accept losing a run now and then."}}